  "conclusions": [
    "Automatic frame-rate correction (frame-duration=0) is not the current default. Setting -1 is expected to be a no-op, not a test of that proposed cause.",
    "Source NTP is SR/PTS reconstruction and does not itself align batch members.",
    "The worker leaves PTS/NTP mux synchronization off and retains independent nonleaky decoded queues.",
    "The current 450 ms skew may be a selection/FIFO offset or bad reconstruction. An independent encoded client does not prove that the worker mapped the same AU correctly.",
    "Exact same-worker AU reference/SEI versus SDK NTP, plus pre-mux arrival ages, are required to separate the causes.",
    "No offset subtraction or guard relaxation is justified."
